# 9. Feature Importance Analysis

The paper does not use feature importance primarily to aggressively reduce the feature set.

Instead, it uses feature importance to understand which variables contribute strongly to the predictions.

The authors use **Random Forest feature importance**.

The important features highlighted in the paper include:

1. Percentage of time with abnormal long-term variability
2. Percentage of time with abnormal short-term variability
3. Histogram Mean

There is an important detail here:

**Histogram Mean was identified as important but was subsequently removed because of its high correlation with other features.**

This demonstrates that feature importance and feature selection are not necessarily the same thing.

Feature importance answers:

> "Which features contribute strongly to the model?"

Feature selection answers:

> "Which features should we retain for modelling?"

The base paper mainly uses the first concept for interpretability and understanding. 

