# 23. Effect of SMOTE

The paper compares model performance before and after SMOTE.

| Model             | Balanced Accuracy Before SMOTE | Balanced Accuracy After SMOTE |
| ----------------- | -----------------------------: | ----------------------------: |
| CatBoost          |                         89.67% |                        91.00% |
| Decision Tree     |                         79.68% |                        84.13% |
| ExtraTrees        |                         83.91% |                        87.88% |
| Gradient Boosting |                         89.42% |                        91.04% |
| KNN               |                         76.76% |                        83.32% |
| LightGBM          |                         90.93% |                        91.34% |
| Random Forest     |                         87.14% |                        89.19% |
| SVM               |                         74.48% |                        82.01% |

The paper reports an average balanced-error-rate reduction of **19.13%** after applying SMOTE.

The largest reported reduction was for SVM at **29.50%**, followed by KNN at **28.23%**.

Importantly, this does **not** mean SVM became the best overall model. It means SVM experienced the largest reported reduction in balanced error rate. LightGBM still had the strongest absolute balanced accuracy after SMOTE among the compared models. 

